offload-bundle-arch: a fix to intel/llvm v7.1.1, applied by tools/intel_llvm_build.py.

A program built for several NVIDIA or AMD architectures got another architecture's device code under each
one's name.  SYCL's bundle IDs carry the GPU without an environment field before it
(sycl-amdgcn-amd-amdhsa-gfx1030), and clang-offload-bundler read it as the triple's environment: the target ID
was empty, every architecture of a triple matched every other, and unbundling an object or an archive gave
each architecture's link the first unclaimed entry of the triple in hash order.  The packages' engine had
gfx1200's code under gfx1030, gfx1030's under gfx1101 and gfx1100's under gfx1201, which an RX 9070 XT
refused as an illegal instruction.  Fixed, a fifth component that names a GPU is the target ID.
---
diff --git a/clang/lib/Driver/OffloadBundler.cpp b/clang/lib/Driver/OffloadBundler.cpp
--- a/clang/lib/Driver/OffloadBundler.cpp
+++ b/clang/lib/Driver/OffloadBundler.cpp
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 // Part of the LLVM Project, under the Apache License v2.0 with LLVM Exceptions.
 // See https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt for license information.
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
+// Modified 2026 by MistVVK and the XeStrata contributors: a SYCL bundle ID's GPU is its target ID (offload-bundle-arch)
 //
 //===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
 ///
@@ -133,6 +134,23 @@
   assert((Components.size() == 5 || Components.size() == 6) &&
          "malformed target string");
 
+  // SYCL's bundle IDs have no environment field before the GPU
+  // (sycl-amdgcn-amd-amdhsa-gfx1030, sycl-nvptx64-nvidia-cuda-sm_75).  Read as
+  // the environment, the GPU left the target ID empty, every architecture of a
+  // triple matched every other, and unbundling gave each one's link another
+  // architecture's device code.
+  if (Components.size() == 5 &&
+      clang::StringToOffloadArch(Components.back().split(':').first) !=
+          clang::OffloadArch::UNKNOWN) {
+    this->OffloadKind = Components.front();
+    this->TargetID = Components.back();
+    ArrayRef<StringRef> TripleSlice{&Components[1], /*length=*/3};
+    llvm::Triple T = llvm::Triple(llvm::join(TripleSlice, "-"));
+    this->Triple = llvm::Triple(T.getArchName(), T.getVendorName(),
+                                T.getOSName(), T.getEnvironmentName());
+    return;
+  }
+
   StringRef TargetIdWithFeature =
       Components.size() == 6 ? Components.back() : "";
   StringRef TargetId = TargetIdWithFeature.split(':').first;
